  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conciliation Resources 2016 - March 2020 - Conciliation Resources 2016 - 2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Conciliation Resources 2016 - mars 2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conciliation Resources is an international NGO working with people in conflict to prevent violence and build peace. This contribution is    for continued core support.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Conciliation Resources &#xe4;r en internationell NGO som specialiserar sig p&#xe5; fredsbyggande. Organisationen har s&#xe4;rskilt profilerat sig genom sitt st&#xf6;d till medling och inkluderande fredsprocesser men arbetar &#xe4;ven v&#xe5;ldsf&#xf6;rebyggande och med policyarbete.  P&#xe5; senare &#xe5;r har organisationen byggt upp en s&#xe4;rskild kompetens vad g&#xe4;ller j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering inom fredsbyggande. Verksamheten sker i bort&#xe5;t ett tjugotal l&#xe4;nder och territorier p&#xe5; flera kontinenter. Insatsen g&#xe4;ller fortsatt k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d om 32,5 MSEK &#xf6;ver fyra &#xe5;r 2016 - 2019.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution will support Conciliation Resources to implement its strategic plan during the period 2016 - 2019. According to this plan, Conciliation Resources will make significant and documented contributions to preventing and transforming violent conflicts and promoting peaceful and inclusive societies.
Moreover,&#xa0;Conciliation Resources has updated their theory of change which is, in the short version, formulated as follows:
&quot;Conciliation Resources aims to develop an environment conducive to and supportive of locally-led peacebuilding (&#x2018;Peace Enablers&#x2019;), in the belief that this will build a foundation for constructive formal and informal peace processes. Peacebuilding initiatives and processes that are both politically sensitive and inclusive will contribute to sustainable and transformative peace outcomes.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
